@name "Namespace does not start with the package's namespace root"
@severity error
@category "Naming"
@description "A type's namespace starts with its assembly name, and for an .Abstractions assembly with the assembly name minus its trailing .Abstractions segment: Bsft.Storage.Abstractions declares Bsft.Storage and Bsft.Storage.Downloads, never Bsft.Storage.Abstractions. An .Abstractions assembly and its implementation share a namespace, so a consumer imports one namespace and a type can move between the two assemblies without a source break. The one exception is the Program class of top-level statements, which the language places in the global namespace."
@recommendation "Declare the namespace as the package's namespace root followed by the folder path. For an .Abstractions package, move every reference along with the namespace; docs/migration-2.0.0.md lists the moves. See docs/package-conventions.md section 3."

from t in Types
where !t.Namespace.Assembly.IsTestProject
where t.FullName != "Program"
where (t.Namespace.Assembly.Name.EndsWith(".Abstractions")
        && (t.Namespace.FullName == t.Namespace.Assembly.Name
            || t.Namespace.FullName.StartsWith(t.Namespace.Assembly.Name + ".")
            || (t.Namespace.FullName != t.Namespace.Assembly.Name.Substring(0, t.Namespace.Assembly.Name.Length - ".Abstractions".Length)
                && !t.Namespace.FullName.StartsWith(t.Namespace.Assembly.Name.Substring(0, t.Namespace.Assembly.Name.Length - ".Abstractions".Length) + "."))))
    || (!t.Namespace.Assembly.Name.EndsWith(".Abstractions")
        && t.Namespace.FullName != t.Namespace.Assembly.Name
        && !t.Namespace.FullName.StartsWith(t.Namespace.Assembly.Name + "."))
select t
